    {
      "text": "Figure 8. (Left) Median loss during the training process for the top performing configuration in each resampling class in the first setting.",
      "bbox": [
        54.893001556396484,
        245.873779296875,
        543.0140991210938,
        253.88973999023438
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "We note that diffusion resampling achieves the lowest loss. (Right) Median loss during the training process for the top performing",
      "bbox": [
        55.01900100708008,
        255.8367919921875,
        541.4437866210938,
        263.8527526855469
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "configuration in each resampling class in the more challenging setting. We note that for OT, the reported median loss is based on the few",
      "bbox": [
        55.439998626708984,
        265.79876708984375,
        541.7644653320312,
        273.8147277832031
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "successful runs and is therefore not statistically meaningful. While Soft achieves the lowest median loss (see the text for discussion),",
      "bbox": [
        55.439998626708984,
        275.76177978515625,
        542.5598754882812,
        283.7777404785156
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "diffusion resampling remains competitive and yields low, stable loss, whereas Gumbel performs markedly worse than all baselines.",
